<div class="row mb-5">
    <div class="col-lg-12">
        <h1 class="display-4 fw-bold mb-3">Product Costing & WIP Valuation</h1>
        <p class="lead mb-4">
            Quantify the true financial heartbeat of your factory floor—tracking actual vs. standard 
            expenditure to identify margin erosion and operational inefficiencies.
        </p>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="row mb-5">
    <div class="col-lg-12">
        <h2 class="h3 fw-bold mb-4">Actual vs. Standard Valuation</h2>
        <p>
            Experience radical financial clarity with dual-view costing. Compare the 'Standard 
            Cost' derived from your Bill of Materials (BOM) against the 'Actual Cost' 
            incurred during a specific production run. The system automatically highlights 
            material usage variances, identifying where excessive scrap or procurement 
            price shifts are impacting job profitability.
        </p>
        <p>
            This surgical view of production expenditure allows for the precise 
            calibration of product pricing and the identification of high-yield 
            operational improvements.
        </p>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="row mb-5">
    <div class="col-lg-12">
        <h2 class="h3 fw-bold mb-4">Labor & Overhead Allocation</h2>
        <p>
            In-depth tracking of labor effort at every work center ensures that actual employment 
            costs are accurately reflected in the product valuation. The software 
            facilitates the sophisticated allocation of factory overheads—such as utilities, 
            rent, and maintenance—across production orders based on machine hours or 
            labor intensity. This move from simple estimates to empirical costing is 
            critical for enterprise-grade financial reporting and auditing.
        </p>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="row mb-5">
    <div class="col-lg-12">
        <h2 class="h3 fw-bold mb-4">Work-in-Progress (WIP) Financials</h2>
        <p>
            Automatically value your floor-based assets. The system maintains a continuous 
            valuation of 'Work-in-Progress' (WIP), aggregating the value of materials 
            issued, labor absorbed, and overheads applied to open production orders. 
            Direct integration with the central ERP General Ledger ensures that 
            manufacturing activity is instantly reflected in the organization's 
            consolidated balance sheet, providing the transparency needed for 
            executive stewardship.
        </p>
    </div>
</div>

